<article class="env-lemma" id="067U">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/067U">Lemma <span data-tag="067U">31.23.11</span>.</a> Let </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  \xymatrix{ Y \ar[rd] \ar[rr]_ i &  &  X \ar[ld] \\  &  S }  \]
</div>
  <p> be a commutative diagram of morphisms of schemes. Assume that $Y \to S$ is smooth, $X \to S$ smooth, and $i$ an immersion. Then $i$ is a regular immersion. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      This is a special case of Lemma <a href="/tag/067T" data-tag="067T">31.23.10</a> because a smooth morphism is syntomic, see Morphisms, Lemma <a href="/tag/01VD" data-tag="01VD">29.35.7</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>